    "description": "Give form_id, respondent_id, answers (questionId to value) and records: the form's question-sequence record and, for deciding the segment, the score-rule, segment-rule and follow-up-sequence records, as a store lists them. Optionally submission_id (for a form answered again and again, so each time has its own records) and answered_at. The answers are checked against the form as check-form-answers does. If any is invalid the first to fix is returned and no records. Otherwise it returns the decision (score and segment), the segment's follow-up sequence, and records: an answer fact for each answer the form asks about, one segment assignment, and one request record for each question whose afterSaved names an owner and action, with the answers filled into its input. Nothing is kept: write the returned records to a store to keep them.",
